  "question": {
    "text": "A small point of mass $m$ is placed at a distance $2 R$ from the centre ' $O^{\\prime}$ of a big uniform solid sphere of mass M and radius R . The gravitational force on ' m ' due to M is $\\mathrm{F}_1$. A spherical part of radius $\\mathrm{R} / 3$ is removed from the big sphere as shown in the figure and the gravitational force on m due to remaining part of M is found to be $\\mathrm{F}_2$. The value of ratio $\\mathrm{F}_1: \\mathrm{F}_2$ is\n\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/RDgeUFlbNVcGwIS91jCJcAxMlBJ5UuncVuYJJ-tDRVo.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
